+
+## 9. spec-replay plan (round 2) — A/B choice and mmproj expectation
+
+- **A = `--spec-type ngram-mod` (defaults).** Same backend that
+  `docs/engine-review.md` already measured on a single slot (61.0 vs 61.5
+  tok/s fresh, 162 tok/s repeated, +4 MiB), so A isolates the *new*
+  conditions: `-np 2`, `--kv-unified`, production agent+mem traffic, and the
+  dual-slot case.
+- **B = `--spec-type ngram-cache` (defaults).** Justification for the second
+  setting: it is the only ngram *type* (not a variant of ngram-mod's draft
+  size) left in the flag list
+  (`none, draft-simple, draft-eagle3, draft-mtp, draft-dflash, draft-dspark,
+  ngram-simple, ngram-map-k, ngram-map-k4v, ngram-mod, ngram-cache`),
+  and it is the one that is explicitly documented as a caching ngram variant
+  (`--spec-ngram-cache`), i.e. a different algorithm with its own acceptance
+  dynamics rather than a re-tune of A. It is therefore the most informative
+  *second point*, not a noise re-run of the same variant. (ngram-simple/map-k/
+  map-k4v are excluded because they are the "simple" family with the smaller
+  12/48 default sizes — same shape as ngram-mod at smaller n/m.)
+- **mmproj expectation.** §3 (static) says spec is usable with `--mmproj`
+  loaded (no mctx gate in the spec gates; mmproj only disables
+  `ctx_shift`/`cache_reuse`). The replay is **text-only** (no images), so the
+  known runtime refusal (`unsupported batch.has_embd + spec case`,
+  server-context.cpp:3550-3553) should *not* fire; the probe therefore expects
+  `draft_n > 0` / `draft_n_accepted > 0` on A and B. Any config with draft
+  0 everywhere is treated as a refusal only if the server log says so (lines
+  quoted in `notes.txt`), and triggers the `-nommproj` rerun per the item.
+- **Per-request max_tokens** = max(recorded `predicted_n`, floor) — floor 768
+  agent, 1024 mem; capped mem0-r0/2/0 stays at 2048 (recorded cap). Identical
+  in every arm so `predicted_per_second` and output identity are comparable
+  (standing facts, round 12).
+- **Analysis rule (advisor).** Count `finish_reason=length` per arm and report
+  speedups with and without capped/looping outputs; greedy looping inflates
+  n-gram gains.
